  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA multiprofile with avgpool is the strongest setting so far (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), while transformer aggregation is weaker and image-only models are weak (accuracy ~0.21-0.23). The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve on PCA in this best profile/aggregation setting. config_008 keeps the proven multiprofile + avgpool design and changes only the RNA encoder to scgpt, testing whether a pretrained single-cell foundation model adds useful signal. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest RNA direction, isolates the representation choice, and either produces a stronger base model or confirms PCA before spending budget on multimodal fusion."
